Article 3 (Standards for the Execution and Management of Local Subsidies)
(1) The Minister of the Interior and Safety shall ensure that every stage of the local subsidy process, including applications, grants, execution, and settlement of accounts, is managed through the Integrated Local Subsidy Management System.
(2) The Integrated Local Subsidy Management System shall include the following matters relating to local subsidy management information under Article 28 (2) of the Act on the Management of Local Government Subsidies:
1. Local subsidy project operators and local subsidy recipients;
2. Where a local subsidy project operator enters into a contract related to a local subsidy project, the other party to the contract.
(3) The Minister of the Interior and Safety shall ensure that the execution of local subsidies is clearly classified and managed in the Integrated Local Subsidy Management System according to the following types:
1. Where a local government, as a local subsidy project operator, directly executes local subsidies;
2. Where a local subsidy project operator executes local subsidies by entering into a contract with a third party in relation to a local subsidy project;
3. Where a local subsidy project operator directly grants and executes local subsidies to a local subsidy recipient on condition that the recipient performs a project or achieves specified outcomes;
4. Other cases where a local subsidy project operator directly grants and executes local subsidies to a local subsidy recipient.
